esponding homogeneous equation, and ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nIn this case, we're told that the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\,{y}_{2}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our expression for ${y}_{p},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}={u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))^{′}+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))^{′}.\n$$\n\nWe can form a constraint that relates ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}$ by differentiating ${y}_{p}$ and equating this expression to our constraint on ${y}_{p}^{′}.$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x$ using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ={({u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}^{′} \\\\  & ={({u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))}^{′}+{({u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))}^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we equate our two expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ={u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))^{′}+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))^{′} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & =5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\cancel{5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\cancel{5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)} & =\\cancel{5{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}-\\cancel{5{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich finally gives\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072088/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e719c887a128c0a6949089ba63db9ef7521e1b3df30b73804e06fe206de6ca2"} {"question" "q-337944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe4b3521ac9b8647f748f028499cb52dbe7956058ad919c2e467dbcc955fb93"} {"question" "q-337944" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072088/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e719c887a128c0a6949089ba63db9ef7521e1b3df30b73804e06fe206de6ca2"} {"question" "q-337944" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))^{′}+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))^{′}"] ["math" "{u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x))^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))^{′}"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072088/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e719c887a128c0a6949089ba63db9ef7521e1b3df30b73804e06fe206de6ca2"} {"question" "q-337944" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+{u}_